## What the author owns

Order and braiding of the four tracks; the cohort's personalities around Ephram (no new names — "four of Rooke's cohort"); Lira's practice bout; the Lattice pupil's manner; the apparatus's small sounds; Karis's delight in the library committee's charter; Seln's walk through the campus as a positioning problem. Humor: Brom's sincerity about being hit; Lira's "That's not a comfort, it's a correction."

## Where we leave pressure

A permanent baseline in Gault's hand: two capabilities, honestly measured, with a shoulder aching till the weekend. Nineteen weeks to the semester evaluation. Ephram has made himself the judge. Brom is being made worse on purpose. Lira is caged. And a teaching assistant who doesn't look at him has a card on the staff corridor: *Seln. Shadow. Bronze.* "Filed."

